@startuml sequence-pdf-refresh-in-place
'' PlantUML over Mermaid: a live refresh of a shown PDF is a race between the reader's position, the bytes in the
'' byte cache and pdf.js, and what makes it safe is the ORDER — the new document is prepared beside the old one,
'' swapped in only once pdf.js has opened it, and the old proxy destroyed only after the swap; a failure at any
'' stage leaves the last good document mounted. A sequence diagram with alt branches states that ordering exactly,
'' and PlantUML takes every participant's colour from the shared theme and renders byte-reproducibly (README §4).
'' Colours, from the shared palette: tan = the file being written; slate = main (one verified read per change,
'' ADR-0046); amber = the IPC seam; blue = re-frame events; purple = DataScript; teal = the renderer's PDF view,
'' its byte cache and the pdf.js engine; red = a failure kept non-fatal.
!include _vv-theme.iuml

title Live refresh in place (ADR-0045): the new PDF swaps in under the same view, on the same slide

autonumber "0:"

participant "writer\n(pdflatex, latexmk)" as W FS_TINT
participant "main\n(watcher · content-flight ·\nverified reader, ADR-0046)" as M MAIN_TINT
participant "preload\nwindow.vv" as P IPC_TINT
participant "re-frame events\n(:content/received ·\n:content/error)" as RF REFRAME_TINT
participant "DataScript\n(:doc/stamp :doc/seq\n:doc/refresh-note :doc/deck)" as DS DATASCRIPT_TINT
participant "pdf-cache\n(byte cache:\ngood · candidate)" as C RENDERER_TINT
participant "pdf-view\n(keyed pdf:<tab>:<path>,\nno stamp)" as V RENDERER_TINT
participant "refresh-note banner\n(ui/refresh-note)" as B RENDERER_TINT
participant "warm cache +\npdf.js (prepare!)" as J RENDERER_TINT
participant "PDF engine\n(renderer.pdf)" as E RENDERER_TINT

== a change: main reads the file once, verified ==
W -> M : rewrites talk.pdf in place
activate M
M -> M : one read per path (content-flight); tail first,\nthen body, fstat, verdict; settle a torn file after\n<latex>u, 2u, 4u, 8u</latex> (<latex>u = 250\,\mathrm{ms}</latex>) — or stay pending for the next change
alt the PDF is complete
  M -[IPC_BORDER]> P : **vv:content** {path, kind "pdf", bytes, seq, stamp}
  deactivate M
  P -> RF : [:content/received payload]
  activate RF
  RF -> RF : content-guard: is seq no newer than the\napplied :doc/seq? → drop it whole (never backwards)
  RF -> C : [:pdf/cache-bytes {path bytes stamp}]\n→ put-bytes! as the CANDIDATE (good kept)
  RF -> DS : :doc/stamp ← stamp, :doc/seq ← seq;\nretract a stale refresh note
  deactivate RF
  DS --> V : re-render with the new stamp — the SAME\ninstance (its key has no stamp): no remount
  activate V
  V -> V : pdf-view-lifecycle/update-actions\n→ the actions :update and :refresh
  V -> E : pdf/update! the view state (always)
  V -> J : refresh!: prepare the candidate beside\nthe live document (a new warm-cache lease)
  note right of E #E3F2ED: the old document stays on screen,\nand the reader keeps scrolling or flipping
  alt pdf.js opens the candidate
    J --> V : {:doc :sizes :deck}
    V -> E : **replace-doc!**
    activate E
    E -> E : keep the anchor (in the Slides layout: the slide);\ncancel tasks, :gen + 1, :doc-gen + 1; grow or shrink\nthe placeholders; relayout; restore the anchor
    E -> E : the visible canvases stay, CSS-stretched; each\nre-render rasterizes into a DETACHED canvas and\nreplaces the old one only when complete
    deactivate E
    V -> J : release the previous lease → destroys the old\nPDFDocumentProxy (only now, after the swap)
    V -> C : promote! — the candidate becomes the good version
    V -> RF : [:pdf/deck-detected path stamp summary]\n[:pdf/refreshed path stamp]
    RF -> DS : :doc/deck (only if changed);\nretract a "render-failed" note
  else pdf.js cannot open it (a corrupt or torn file)
    J -[ERROR_BORDER]-> V : rejected
    V -> J : release the candidate's lease
    V -> C : reject! — drop the candidate, keep the good version
    V -[ERROR_BORDER]> RF : [:pdf/refresh-failed path stamp message]
    RF -[ERROR_BORDER]> DS : :doc/refresh-note {:kind "render-failed"}
    DS --> B : the :doc/refresh-note subscription → the banner shows
    note right of E #F5E1E0: the last good render stays mounted;\nthe banner offers Retry and ×
  end
  deactivate V
else stable but incomplete — this window shows a complete version
  M -[IPC_BORDER]> P : **vv:content** {…, seq, incomplete, incompleteReason}
  P -> RF : [:content/received payload]
  RF -[ERROR_BORDER]> DS : only :doc/refresh-note {:kind "incomplete"} and :doc/seq —\nno stamp, no candidate: the view is not touched
  DS --> B : the banner shows
else main cannot read it (deleted, refused, a dropped SSH connection)
  M -[IPC_BORDER]> P : **vv:error** {path, message, seq, refresh}
  P -> RF : [:content/error payload]
  RF -[ERROR_BORDER]> DS : :doc/refresh-note {:kind "refresh-failed"} and :doc/seq —\nnever :doc/error, so nothing remounts
  DS --> B : the banner shows
end

== Retry on the banner ==
B -> RF : Retry → [:doc/refresh-retry path] → [:vv/open path]
RF -[IPC_BORDER]> P : **vv:open** path
P -[IPC_BORDER]> M : main re-reads; the next applied read clears the note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Concept |
  |<#9F8766>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the file being written |
  |<#3A5BA0>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| main: one verified, numbered read per change (ADR-0046) |
  |<#B1951D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| IPC seam |
  |<#4F97D7>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| re-frame events |
  |<#A45BAD>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| DataScript document entity |
  |<#2D9574>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| renderer: pdf-view, byte cache, banner, pdf.js, PDF engine |
  |<#E0211D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| a failure, kept non-fatal behind the refresh note |
  A PDF with nothing complete to keep shows what pdf.js can recover (or the error page).
endlegend
@enduml
